{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall give it to Elazar the priest.</b> This one is performed by Elazar, as Rashi explained, while all other cows are performed whether by a high priest or by an ordinary priest. And one may say, according to the plain sense: since it contaminates all who are occupied with it, HaShem did not wish the high priest to be contaminated by it. Here Rashi explained that its commandment is through the deputy — meaning the deputy was the overseer and in charge of all its affairs. One may say: it requires seven priests to perform it, for the seven matters in it — and he brought out, and slaughtered, and took from its blood, and burned the cow, and took cedar wood, and gathered — a pure man, and placed the ash outside the camp." "<b>And he shall bring it out.</b> It is a short verse — it did not specify who brings it out, and likewise 'and slaughter,' 'and burn,' 'and gather,' 'and place.' <b>And he shall slaughter it before him</b> — before Elazar. Here Rashi explained: a non-priest slaughters and Elazar watches — meaning a deputy is not required to slaughter it, and an ordinary priest slaughters it, for he is a non-priest with respect to several services imposed on the deputy. And a parallel to this we find in the chapter יש נוחלין: he considered it actual foreign worship, and he does not know a service that is foreign to him — and that is according to Rabbi Yitzchak, who said in the chapter טרף בקלפי: slaughter of the cow by a non-priest is invalid."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:36.627837858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}